"""
==============================================================================
CvC / PvP PRICING & PORTFOLIO PROJECT -- CAC40 vs S&P500 SECTOR BASKETS
==============================================================================
Single self-contained script. Run directly in VS Code
("Run Python File" button, or `python cvc_pvp_project.py` in the terminal).

TRADES COVERED
--------------
    1. CAC Tech    (Capgemini / Dassault Systemes / STMicroelectronics)
       vs S&P Tech (Nvidia / Microsoft / Alphabet)
    2. CAC Energy  (TotalEnergies / Engie)
       vs S&P Energy (ExxonMobil / Chevron)
    3. CAC Luxury  (LVMH / Hermes / Kering / L'Oreal)
       vs S&P Media (Disney / Comcast / Netflix / Warner Bros Discovery)

Each sector basket is also compared to a sector reference index (MSCI
World proxy: IT, Energy, Luxury/Consumer Discretionary, Communication
Services).

WHAT THIS SCRIPT DOES
----------------------
1. Loads market data (tries Yahoo Finance via yfinance; falls back
   automatically to a calibrated 3-factor market simulation if no
   internet connection is available -- e.g. sandboxed environments).
2. Builds the 6 equity baskets listed above.
3. Runs a full correlation analysis, basket by basket (static matrix +
   60-day rolling correlation), including basket vs sector benchmark.
4. Prices the 3 CvC / PvP trades via Monte Carlo (correlated multi-asset
   GBM, antithetic variates), with the closed-form Margrabe formula
   included as a 2-asset reference check.
5. Plots the "correlation vega" (price sensitivity to correlation) for
   each trade -- the key risk of these structures.
6. Aggregates everything into a portfolio, with total value and a 95%
   Value-at-Risk.
7. Compares each sector basket to its MSCI-proxy benchmark.
8. DISPLAYS every chart on screen as it is generated, saves all of them
   as high-resolution PNGs to ./output/figures/, prints every table to
   the console, and writes a full Markdown report to
   ./output/reports/report.md.

REQUIREMENTS
------------
pip install numpy pandas matplotlib seaborn scipy yfinance tabulate

NOTE ON DATA
------------
If you run this with an internet connection, real Yahoo Finance data
will be used automatically (5 years of daily history) -- no code change
needed. Without internet, the script falls back to a factor-model
simulation calibrated to produce realistic CAC40 / S&P500 / sector
correlations, so the methodology and all charts remain fully valid for
demonstration purposes.
==============================================================================
"""

